@startuml create-wireframe
|User|
start
:Open the application;
|Storage|
:Restore the project library;
|User|
if (Start from?) then (empty library: Create project)
  |Editor|
  :Create "Untitled project" with one empty screen
  and open it;
else (open project: Add screen)
  |Editor|
  :Create an empty screen with a generated name
  and open it;
endif
|Editor|
:Show a prompt explaining how to add
the first component;
|User|
:Choose a component from the palette;
|Editor|
:Insert it into the empty screen,
then select and focus it;
|User|
:Change its properties with visible controls;
|Editor|
:Update the canvas and the screen's source;
|Renderer|
if (Render succeeds?) then (yes)
  :Show the rendered preview;
else (no)
  :Keep the last preview, marked out of date,
  and show the rendering problem;
endif
|User|
if (Share the work?) then (download project)
  |Editor|
  :Download the project as one .puml file;
  |Storage|
  :Record the last-downloaded time;
elseif (Share the work?) then (export image)
  |Editor|
  :Export the screen as SVG or PNG;
else (not yet)
  |Storage|
  :Autosave the project;
endif
|User|
stop
@enduml
